---
import ProjectDetailLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectDetailLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "../../utils/withBase";
import { getProject } from "../../data/projects";

const project = getProject("stocksinseconds");
---

<ProjectDetailLayout
  title={project.name}
  heading={`${project.name} (Taken offline)`}
>
  <div class="projectDetailMedia projectDetailMedia--bordered">
    <img
      src={withBase(project.image)}
      alt={project.imageAlt}
      class="projectDetailImage"
    />
  </div>
  <section class="projectDetailPanel">
    <p>
      StocksInSeconds.com is a website for a startup company. I developed the
      backend along with the communications on the frontend. I was able to use
      my knowledge of python and javascript but I had to learn many technologies
      for this project such as Flask API, some AWS, NoSQL, user authentication
      and authorization, cookies, domains, and more.
    </p>
    <p>
      I created the backend in python Flask then realized I needed to host it
      somewhere. I did research and decided that AWS was the best fit for my
      scenaria. The code development was somewhat simple but the other parts
      such as SSL/TLS certificates were more challenging because I did not know
      how to do most of it. I had to learn about how authentication works,
      cookies, HTTPS and SSL/TLS certificates, DNS management, cloud computing,
      and basic security concepts. Each of these topics helped me learn a lot
      about web development and how to make a secure website.
    </p>
    <p>
      Overall I learned a lot about many aspects of web development. Obviously,
      I learned some about site development and deployment, but more importantly
      I learned about lots of security concepts. This project got me interested
      in penetration testing and ethical hacking after all the research I had
      to do about web security. I am proud of how this project turned out, but
      sadly it was taken offline by the owners due to a lack of time to develop
      the other parts of the business.
    </p>
  </section>
</ProjectDetailLayout>
